 "gaps": [],
 "footnotes": [
  "p. 18 n. 1 (on Àusàr, Pl. IV l. 3): In British Museum papyrus No. 9901 [Hunefer], the speech of Horus reads:— prints a parallel text in hieroglyphs, 3 rows, with transliteration (t'et àn Ḥeru net' tef-f uā menχ en Un-nefer mākuà ḥer bes-nek Àusàr Hu-nefer àu-f sàp mā māχa àu pa teχ hui er àuset-f) and translation 'Saith Horus the avenger of his father, heir veritable of Un-nefer: I am come to lead to thee Osiris Hu-nefer. He hath been judged in the scales, the weight of the balance resteth (?) upon its place.'"
 ],
 "notes": "p. 17 opens in Pl. III l. 27 (Ani maāχeru). On p. 17 l. 28 the numeral 29 falls inside Āmemet (between X1 and the beast determinative); the word is given line 28. Plate IV starts at the heading on p. 17; ll. 1-3 there, p. 18 continues l. 3 (àmmā) to l. 9 (enti); p. 19 continues l. 9 (àm-χet-k) and l. 10 down to χer Àusàr above 'PLATE V.'. Rubric overlines: p. 17 Pl. IV l. 1 over t'eṭ àn Ḥeru (ends before se); p. 18 l. 5 over the untransliterated cobra group and àn (not Àusàr); p. 18 l. 6 over t'eṭ - f only. No overlines on p. 17 Pl. III rows or p. 19. No hatching or gaps in my range. On p. 18 l. 5 Budge prints no transliteration under the first (cobra) group: entry with empty budge. Ani's determinative varies: chair+flail (A51) on p. 17 l. 27, Pl. IV l. 1, p. 19 l. 10; squatting with flail (A52) on p. 18 l. 5. Budge's 'àn' (decree, p. 17 l. 2) and 'ān' (scribe, p. 19) are the same scribe's-outfit sign Y3. The 'm' of embaḥ / māk / àmmā (p. 18 l. 9) is Aa15, sometimes doubled. 'àn' negation is D35 (+N35), different from àn of speech (M17 N35)."
}